    <item>
      <title>Populism’s Next Chapter Is Being Written in Continental Europe</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-23/populism-s-next-chapter-is-being-written-in-continental-europe</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7d5d5da02c9c6afb01956a78</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Since 2016, the story of populism in the rich world has been dominated by the Anglo-Saxons — by Britain’s vote for Brexit and America’s decision to elect Donald Trump not once (which might have been put down to naiveté) but twice. But things are about to change: Over the next year populism is likely to fade in the Anglo-Saxon world but burn ever brighter in continental Europe.</description>
      <dc:creator>Adrian Wooldridge</dc:creator>
