      <title>AI Efficiencies Can Stifle Corporate Innovation</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-23/ai-efficiencies-can-stifle-corporate-innovation</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">aa136ddc05f8ea2032c0a15a</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:30:11 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The latest way to sell artificial intelligence is with a high-tech version of the promise that corporate America last bought from Six Sigma. Earlier this month, Workday Inc. told investors that its customers should pay for its AI agents out of what they spend on labor and services, not just software. Workday itself, its CEO said, was looking to replace new hires with AI.</description>
      <dc:creator>Gautam Mukunda</dc:creator>
