      <title>Meta’s Muse Can’t Be a Freeloader’s Paradise Forever</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-23/meta-s-muse-can-t-be-a-freeloader-s-paradise-forever</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">bc755250cff9fdbdae1dcd38</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:30:13 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>When I introduced my mother to Uber, she asked whether it was always the same driver.   Imagine that! Some poor guy waiting around all day on the off chance I’d need a car. Uber’s innovation, obviously, was to pair me with any available driver nearby. Only then was it economical — and it still took more than a decade for the idea to turn a profit.</description>
      <dc:creator>Dave Lee</dc:creator>
